ived_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@andrea-agostini My understanding is that SeaweedFS has two TTL mechanisms: one for the metadata database of the `filer server` and another for the volumes on the `volume server`. The TTL set in `fs.configure` will assign a TTL to the volume when files are uploaded. After this, the volume server will trigger the deletion of the volume through a scheduled mechanism. However, the expiration deletion of the metadata on the filer server requires a `list` or `get` operation to be triggered.","created_at":"2024-08-09T00:40:37Z","updated_at":"2024-08-09T00:40:37Z","html_url":"https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pull/5783#discussion_r1710497552","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pulls/5783","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pulls/comments/1710497552"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pull/5783#discussion_r1710497552"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pulls/5783"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pulls/comments/1710497552/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":337,"original_line":337,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1708886399,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":1,"subject_type":"line","is_copilot_code_review":false,"copilot_code_review_sources":[]},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/pulls/comments/1710498930","pull_request_review_id":2229097422,"id":1710498930,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAU0OSs5l9CRy","diff_hunk":"@@ -334,7 +334,10 @@ func (f *Filer) FindEntry(ctx context.Context, p util.FullPath) (entry *Entry, e\n \tentry, err = f.Store.FindEntry(ctx, p)\n \tif entry != nil && entry.TtlSec > 0 {\n \t\tif entry.Crtime.Add(time.Duration(entr